  "statement": "Given two integers n and k, return _an array of all the integers of length_ `n` _where the difference between every two consecutive digits is_ `k`. You may return the answer in **any order**.\n\nNote that the integers should not have leading zeros. Integers as `02` and `043` are not allowed.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 3, k = 7\nOutput: [181,292,707,818,929]\nExplanation: Note that 070 is not a valid number, because it has leading zeroes.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 2, k = 1\nOutput: [10,12,21,23,32,34,43,45,54,56,65,67,76,78,87,89,98]\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `2 <= n <= 9`\n*   `0 <= k <= 9`",
  "constraints": [
    "2 <= n <= 9",
    "0 <= k <= 9"
  ],
  "examples": [
